WCD = (hop_count \* (switching_delay + propagation_delay + time_synchronization_error)) + (payload / bandwidth) + (cycle_duration \* (queue_size / bandwidth))

where:

* hop_count is the number of hops in the path
* switching_delay, propagation_delay, and time_synchronization_error are the delays introduced by the switch, propagation, and time synchronization, respectively
* payload is the size of the payload in bytes
* bandwidth is the bandwidth of the link in bits per second
* cycle_duration is the duration of the cycle in microseconds
* queue_size is the maximum payload size of all flows in the queue

Note that the queue_size is assumed to be the maximum payload size of all flows in the queue, which may not be accurate in all cases. Therefore, the confidence level is set to 0.8, indicating that the calculation is based on the given information and assumptions, but may not be entirely accurate.

